course: dictionary
lesson: 5311
title: Using context to find a word's meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «The kea is a clever, curious mountain parrot from New Zealand.» Parrot, mountain and New Zealand are your clues, so a kea must be a bird that lives high up in the hills.
explain: Watch out for names. «Mount Everest is the highest mountain above sea level; Mauna Kea, a volcano in Hawaii, is taller measured from its base on the sea floor.» Here kea is part of a place name, not a bird. Context tells you which meaning is right every time.
explain: Look for clues about what the word does. «The kea is famous for pulling apart cars, bags and tents.» Pulling things apart tells you a kea is cheeky and clever. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A kea is a large, olive-green mountain parrot from the South Island of New Zealand.
fact: Keas have bright orange feathers under their wings, which show when they fly.
fact: Keas are famous for being very clever and cheeky, and they love solving puzzles.
fact: Keas are endangered, so they are protected.
fact: Mauna Kea is a volcano in Hawaii, so it is a place name, not a bird.
exercise: «A kea is a large, olive-green mountain parrot.» What is a kea? | *A parrot | A type of car | A volcano in Hawaii | A kind of mountain rock
exercise: «The kea pulled the cap off the tourist's bag.» What does this show about keas? | *They are cheeky and clever | They are shy and quiet | They cannot fly | They only eat grass
exercise: «Mauna Kea, a volcano in Hawaii, is taller than Everest from its base.» What kind of thing is Mauna Kea? | A bag of food | *A volcano | A kind of car | A parrot
test: Where do keas live? | Under the sea | In the deserts of Australia | *On the mountains of New Zealand's South Island | In the cities of Hawaii
test: What colour are the feathers under a kea's wings? | *Bright orange | White | Black | Blue
exam: Why is the kea called «the clown of the mountains»? | Because it wears a red nose | *Because it plays and pulls things apart, like a clown | Because it cannot fly | Because it sings only in the city
